  "prefLabel": "Mec 404.01 Obligation to Complete Continuing Education",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Mec 404.01 Obligation to Complete Continuing Education.\n\n(a) To be eligible for licensure renewal, individual mechanical licensees shall complete a total of no fewer than 6 hours of continuing education for each plumbing or fuel gas fitting endorsement, in every 2 year licensing cycle, given by:\n\n(1) A board approved seminar provider described in Mec 404.02, teaching a continuing education seminar described in Mec 404.03; or\n\n(2) A comprehensive training session sanctioned by the board, if the licensee is personally a board approved seminar provider.\n\nSource. #10848, eff 7-1-15; ss by #13771, eff 12-10-23 (formerly Saf-Mec 404.01) (see Revision Note at chapter heading for Mec 400)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/mec400.html"
